{
  "question": "A new LTC resident arrived without meds, and their first fill rejects with 01642. Which override applies?",
  "status": "answered",
  "assumption": "Assuming NY Medicaid (NYRx), since 01642 is an eMedNY Early Fill Overuse edit and the question is a claim rejection.",
  "answer": "Assuming NY Medicaid: use the **New Patient Processing override**, not Leave of Absence.\n\n1. Confirm you're an LTC-servicing pharmacy and eligibility returns \"NH\" (the member is a recent admit to a SNF or health-related facility).\n2. Confirm the 01642 (or 02242) denial is the first dispensing of that drug, strength and directions after admission.\n3. Resubmit with Reason for Service Code (439-E4) **NP** and Submission Clarification Code **18** (LTC Patient Admit/Readmit).\n4. Day supply is limited to 30 days unless the drug is subject to short-cycle billing.\n\nYou can't use this override if any condition isn't met. In that case, call the Department. Community pharmacies should also call the Department.",
